comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T05:03:09.191Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"Failure -> cause -> fix: cross-window string true expected handler invalid_input -> GH-1665 host normalization in pm-cli 2026.11.8 -> assert normalized success, replace refusal with invalid boolean host extension_flag_value_invalid (exit 2), retain reachable empty-left handler invalid_input and prove no history writes. Public compareQuantities raw-value refusals remain relevant to direct domain API callers. Baseline focused test reproduced 3 pass / 1 fail before adaptation; no production functions changed, so behavioral function revert is inapplicable."
  "2026-11-14T05:03:36.912Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,Focused cross-window regression passes 4/4. Running npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds; exact final-head CI will supply remaining evidence if a gate exceeds its time budget.
  "2026-11-14T05:14:15.774Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,The initial local release gate exposed clone merge-driver drift after the host upgrade. Reinstalled the current merge mapping and retain its generated repository-relative .gitattributes fence; tracker health then passes. This is toolchain configuration only; no history re-anchoring or source changes. Coverage and remaining npm/Bun release gates run at unchanged thresholds.
  "2026-11-14T05:37:37.927Z",codex-toolchain-1114b,"| Failure | Cause (changelog) | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| cross-window harness string true expected invalid_input | pm-cli 2026.11.8 GH-1665 normalizes declared option values | assert normalized success; replace refusal with invalid boolean host code/exit 2 and empty-left handler code/exit 2; retain no history writes |\n\nLocal npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass. Each runs 95/95 tests, all four coverage dimensions at 100 percent over eight emitted sources, packed acceptance 1/1, and 55 expected behavioral failures followed by passing restored checks. Focused cross-window regression passes 4/4. Bun gate uses isolated HOME and Git configuration. Upstream candidate (not filed): pm-cli 2026.11.13 passes options {enabled: []} through a declared strict boolean flag into a synthetic handler; expected extension_flag_value_invalid with exitCode 2. This is an unclassified validation gap, not a proven new regression. The package retains public domain validation of raw arrays and remains correct if the host later refuses first."
